    "b-60-knowledge-the-knowledge-system-org-1": {
      "id": "b-60-knowledge-the-knowledge-system-org-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The knowledge system organizes what the harness knows, how each kind of knowledge stays true, and how workers consume it. Read this section in order from maintenance principles and target-scoped structures through stores, inputs, worker surfaces, background jobs, and the design record. Its children form a taxonomy by maintenance regime: who keeps each kind of knowledge true. The end-to-end process spine lives in the Process Overview child."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-60-knowledge-design-record-recove-2": {
      "id": "b-60-knowledge-design-record-recove-2",
      "type": "quote",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Design record — recovered v14 · implemented 2026-08-11.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " This design is implemented and live: the librarian is the single knowledge agent, the ledger holds the backfilled knowledge base, the per-target indexes are built each epoch, and the knowledge tab serves it all. This bundle remains the design record; resolved decisions and implementation history live under Record, while as-built documentation lives in the implementation knowledge section."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
